# Godot 4+ generated/cache files - safe to ignore, Godot rebuilds these automatically
.godot/
.import/
export.cfg

# export_presets.cfg is deliberately NOT ignored. It is not a cache file - Godot
# never regenerates it, and its include_filter is load-bearing: a plain .cfg is
# not a resource, so Models/Suspects/suspect_models.cfg only reaches the .pck
# because that filter names it. With this file ignored, a fresh clone exported a
# cast of black silhouettes walking backwards and nobody could see why. Its
# codesign identity and Apple team ID are empty, so there is nothing secret in it.

# Common OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp

# Godot exported builds (if you ever export to a folder inside the project)
/builds/
/export/

# --- exported builds go to GitHub Releases, never into git -----------------
# The Godot 4.7 Windows *release* template is 104.39 MiB on its own, so a
# release build can never be pushed: GitHub hard-rejects any file over 100 MiB.
# The builds that did fit here were debug exports, which is not what should
# reach a player. Releases take 2GB per file and cost nothing, so:
#     gh release create vX.Y.Z executibles/*
# Keep the folder - the export presets write into it - just never commit it.
executibles/

# --- generated training material, all local-only -------------------------
# None of this belongs on GitHub: the harvests and datasets are hundreds of
# megabytes, the character briefs give away every suspect's secret, the play
# logs print the murderer at the top, and the model file is 2.1GB.
TrainingData/
Training/__pycache__/
Training/prompts.txt
Training/PLAYBOOK.md
Training/RUNS.md
Training/Manual/
Training/Modelfile/
Training/_probe_*.txt
JudgePackets/
RewritePackets/
DialogueLogs/
sft.jsonl
dpo.jsonl
dpo_needs_chosen.jsonl
eval_report.md
probe_*.md
*.gguf
ArchibaldModelfile*

# Scratch drawer for files that could not be deleted on a OneDrive mount.
_to_delete/

# --- llama-server engine binary, fetched from upstream, not stored here --
# ~370MB with its bundled CUDA DLLs, and GitHub rejects individual files
# over 100MB regardless. Tools/llama-server-README.md has the exact
# download link, this stays a sibling file so it survives this rule.
Tools/llama-server/
